  {
    "index": 48,
    "sentence": "Write S as a double sum:\n  S = Σₖ₌₂^∞ Σⱼ₌₂^2008 1/j^k.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 49,
    "sentence": "Since the series converges absolutely, we can switch the order of summation:\n  S = Σⱼ₌₂^2008 Σₖ₌₂^∞ 1/j^k.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Analyze"
  },
  {
    "index": 50,
    "sentence": "Step 2.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Monitor"
  },
  {
    "index": 51,
    "sentence": "Evaluate the inner sum for a fixed j:\n  For any fixed j (with j ≥ 2), consider\n    A = Σₖ₌₂^∞ 1/j^k.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Plan"
  },
  {
    "index": 52,
    "sentence": "This is a geometric series with first term 1/j² and common ratio 1/j.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Analyze"
  },
  {
    "index": 53,
    "sentence": "Since |1/j| < 1, the sum is:\n  A = (1/j²) / (1 - 1/j).",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 54,
    "sentence": "Simplify A:\n  A = (1/j²) / ((j - 1)/j) = (1/j²) · (j/(j - 1)) = 1/(j(j - 1)).",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 55,
    "sentence": "Step 3.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Monitor"
  },
  {
    "index": 56,
    "sentence": "Substitute back into S:\n  S = Σⱼ₌₂^2008 1/(j(j - 1)).",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 57,
    "sentence": "Step 4.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Monitor"
  },
  {
    "index": 58,
    "sentence": "Recognize the telescoping form:\n  Notice that\n    1/(j(j - 1)) = 1/(j - 1) - 1/j.",
